
1. Open Visual Studio Code and create a new Flutter project.
2. Open the lib folder and select main.dart.
3. Import the Flutter Material and Dart Convert packages.
4. Create an Employee class with ID, Name and Department.
5. Create a constructor to initialize employee details.
6. Implement toJson() to convert employee details into a Map.
7. Implement fromJson() to convert the Map back into an Employee object.
8. Create an Employee object with ID 201, Name Ravi and Department IT.
9. Create a StatefulWidget to manage application state.
10. Use setState() to add the employee name to a list.
11. Use ListView.builder to display the employee names.
12. Run the application and verify the employee details and JSON output.
